<p>When a hailstorm, microburst, fire, or plumbing failure damages a business property, the insurance claim usually involves more moving parts than a homeowner claim. There may be a building limit, a business personal property limit, business income coverage, and a coinsurance clause, all on the same policy. As a <strong>commercial public adjuster in McAllen</strong>, we help owners and managers in Hidalgo County and the Rio Grande Valley (RGV) document the loss, read the policy, and present the claim clearly. This page explains how commercial claims typically work and where they tend to go wrong.</p>

<h2>Types of Commercial Property Damage We See</h2>
<p>McAllen-area commercial buildings are exposed to the same severe weather as homes, but the construction and the stakes are different. Common losses include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Roof damage</strong> to flat and low-slope systems (TPO, modified bitumen, built-up) and to metal roofs on warehouses and shop buildings. See our <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof damage claims</a> page.</li>
<li><strong>Hail and wind damage</strong> to rooftop HVAC units, skylights, signage, storefront glass, and exterior finishes. The April 28, 2023 wind event, for example, produced NWS-surveyed damage to commercial roofs and walls along W Business 83 in McAllen (<a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1084451" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NOAA NCEI event record</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Water damage</strong> from failed supply lines, sprinkler leaks, and wind-driven rain through damaged roofs.</li>
<li><strong>Fire and smoke</strong> losses in restaurants, retail, and mixed-use buildings. See <a href="/services/fire-damage-claims/">fire damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Contents and inventory</strong> losses, including equipment, fixtures, and stock.</li>
</ul>
<p>We work with retail, office, warehouse and industrial, restaurant, multifamily and apartment, mixed-use, and HOA-managed properties, whether owner-occupied or tenant-occupied.</p>

<h2>Typical Documentation for a Commercial Claim</h2>
<p>Commercial insurers usually ask for more financial and property records than residential carriers. Starting early saves weeks. Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> covers the basics; the table below adds the commercial-specific items.</p>
